From b71a431c79b966fa0f3333b3517232f002f8ab74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:41:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 072/294] pvr, pco: skip the dynamic offset add for non-dynamic
 buffers

Buffer loads, stores and atomics added the descriptor's offset word to
the address with a second add64_32. Only dynamic buffers have a non-zero
offset word there (write_buffer() leaves it 0), so record dynamic
bindings in pco_binding_data and skip the add for the others.

BXM-4-64: cstp 17 -> 16 instruction groups, cstpi 113 -> 112, cstpf
115 -> 114. With the previous commit, interleaved A/B x7 (pinned to the
A76 cores): cstpf 144.8 -> 148.7 M inv/s, cstpi 147.5 -> 151.2 M inv/s;
cstp (bound by per-dispatch overhead) and the graphics tests unchanged.

CTS (synchronization list 1718 + 5062 + 9170 + 838 + 282 cases) was run
with this and the other three commits of this series applied: identical
to before, except one case that ran into the kernel's 500 ms job timeout
(memory.pipeline_barrier.graphics.host_write_vertex_buffer.1048576_vertex_buffer_stride_2,
which passes in 20+ other runs; kernel timeout recovery bug). weston +
weston-simple-egl + vkcube: OK.
